module vtd-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.authority.{ CaseOrder }
import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }

// The District of Vermont's own criminal periods, counted under the
// criminal rules (FRCrimP 45(a) governs "any local rule"). The criminal
// Local Rules supplement the Federal Rules of Criminal Procedure, and the
// court's other Local Rules and the Federal Rules of Civil Procedure
// govern criminal procedures to the extent applicable directly or by
// analogy, unless they conflict with a statute or a Federal Rule of
// Criminal Procedure (D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 1). Which civil Local Rule periods
// apply "by analogy" the rule does not say, so none is encoded here. No
// trigger carries a service method: FRCrimP 45(c)'s three added days
// follow the manner of service, which is not modeled here.
//
// Conditions that are not deadlines from an event stay in notes: the
// court issues its standard Criminal Pretrial Order at arraignment (L. Cr.
// R. 16; not vendored); a Speedy Trial Act continuance needs a motion or
// stipulation stating the exclusion and a proposed order (L. Cr. R.
// 16(g)); sentencing occurs without unnecessary delay under FRCrimP 32 and
// the scheduling orders, whose time limits the court may change for good
// cause (L. Cr. R. 32(a)); and on the day objections to the draft
// presentence report are due (an FRCrimP 32(f)(1) period, in lit/frcrimp)
// the parties exchange undisclosed sentencing information and witnesses
// (L. Cr. R. 16(i)(2)).
//
// The earlier D. Vt. criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions
// (United States v. Salerno, Barker v. Wingo, Zedner v. United States,
// Brady v. Maryland and the others it named) are FRCrimP, Speedy Trial
// Act or constitutional authority and belong to lit/frcrimp; they are
// removed here: no reporter text is vendored.
/// The defendant is arraigned; the court issues its standard Criminal
/// Pretrial Order (D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 16).
event Arraigned()
/// The date set for the start of jury selection (D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 16(d)).
event JurySelectionScheduled()
/// The trial date (D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 16(h)).
event TrialScheduled()
/// The defendant's conviction or guilty plea (D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 32(b)).
event ConvictionOrGuiltyPlea()

/// D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 16(a): unless the court orders otherwise, the
/// government makes available within 14 days of arraignment the FRCrimP
/// 16(a) material with notice under FRCrimP 12(b)(4), Brady material, its
/// case-in-chief witness list, and the search-warrant and electronic
/// surveillance papers.
deadline government-discovery: 14.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 16(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 16(b): a defendant who refuses the FRCrimP
/// 16(a)(1)(E)-(G) materials does so in writing within 5 days of
/// arraignment; otherwise the reciprocal disclosure below is owed.
deadline reciprocal-discovery-refusal: 5.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 16(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 16(b): unless the defendant refused in time, the
/// defendant makes available within 21 days of arraignment all FRCrimP
/// 16(b) material and the names, addresses and birth dates of its
/// case-in-chief witnesses.
deadline defense-discovery: 21.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 16(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 16(c): within 21 days of arraignment, the defendant
/// gives the written notices FRCrimP 12.1, 12.2 and 12.3 require.
deadline defense-notices: 21.days after Arraigned() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 16(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 16(d): unless the court orders otherwise for good
/// cause, not less than 14 days before the start of jury selection the
/// government provides Giglio material and notice of Federal Rule of
/// Evidence 404(b) evidence in its case in chief.
deadline government-pretrial-disclosure: 14.days before JurySelectionScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 16(d)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 16(h)(1): within 3 days of the trial date, counsel for
/// each party exchange and file voir dire requests, requests to charge
/// whose need was not apparent before trial, and a proposed exhibit list;
/// read as 3 days before the trial date. Within the same 3 days counsel
/// make every effort to stipulate facts and admissibility (L. Cr. R.
/// 16(h)(2)).
deadline pretrial-filings: 3.days before TrialScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 16(h)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 32(b): defense counsel, entitled to attend the
/// probation officer's interview of the defendant, must be available for
/// it within 10 days after conviction or guilty plea unless the court
/// grants an extension.
deadline presentence-interview-availability: 10.days after ConvictionOrGuiltyPlea() counted_by frcrimp45 delegable {
  to CaseOrder
  op set
} cite "D. Vt. L. Cr. R. 32(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
